  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes, (2) evaluating which outcomes exceed this level, and (3) preferring the lottery with the higher chance of exceeding it. There is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual computed such a level or evaluated outcomes relative to it. Instead, the individual’s justification is based on risk aversion and the certainty of Lottery B. While both the reason and the individual prefer Lottery B, the underlying rationale differs: the reason relies on outcome-based aspiration and probability of exceeding it, whereas the individual relies on risk avoidance and certainty. The information considered (certainty vs. risk) and the justification (no desire to take risk) do not align with the aspiration-level mechanism. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this specific decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
